### Page 1 of 2

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

June 8, 2021
SUBJECT:
Consideration of Bid #E-29-21 for furnishing One (1) New 2021-2022 Twin-Screw
Diesel Powered Cab & Chassis, for the City of Cheyenne, Sanitation Division
______________________________________________
Four (4) bidders responded to this bid, and the bid tabulation is attached.

The Four (4) Bids were received from:
1. Floyd's Truck Center.  Cheyenne, Wyoming
a. Submitted a NO BID.
2. Peterbilt of Wyoming.  Cheyenne, Wyoming.
a. (Bid in Compliance, No Bid Exceptions Present).
3. Tri-State Truck and Equipment.  Casper, Wyoming.
a. (Bid in Compliance, Bid Exceptions Present).
4. McCandless Truck Center.  Cheyenne, Wyoming.
a. (Bid in Compliance, Bid Exceptions Present).
The bids were reviewed by Vicki Nemecek (Public Works), Craig LaVoy (Public Works), Steven
Pauli (Sanitation), and Bryan Bell (Fleet Maintenance).  Their recommendation is to accept the
lowest responsive bid from Peterbilt of Wyoming, for One (1) New 2021-2022 Twin-Screw Diesel
Powered Cab & Chassis, Less Trade In, Plus 5 Year / 150K Mile Aftermarket Engine &
Aftertreatment Warranty, for a bid award amount of $119,264.00.
Basis for award was determined on Cost/Each, Less Trade In.  After application of the 5%
Preference for Resident Bidders, Peterbilt of Wyoming was determined to be the Lowest
Responsive Bidder, as a Certified Resident Contractor/Supplier.

Funding:
023-14-1417-43-43102 (Solid Waste Fund / Equipment)

Total $119,264.00
```

